cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vidroute in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "vidroute: routing local video to what an agent's LLM can consume"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "vidroute contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/wblearner-mini/vidroute"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wblearner-mini/vidroute"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0.dev0"
keywords:
  - video understanding
  - speech recognition
  - OCR
  - LLM agents
  - Model Context Protocol
abstract: >-
  vidroute decides what to hand an AI agent's language model for a local video — the video itself,
  keyframes with a local transcript, or text — from the model's and the host's capabilities, prepares
  it locally (speech recognition, OCR, keyframes, transcoding) and guides the analysis with global
  timestamps and evidence-based proofreading.
